--- FINDINGS (observations for the lead's backlog, NOT part of the FAIL)
1. The `#whatif-guardrail-anchors` container lives INSIDE the card's
   `{{if and .Settings.Guardrails .Settings.Guardrails.Enabled}}` block
   (guardrails.html:16 / :58), so while guardrails are disabled the page has
   no OOB target and the OOB payload is dropped by htmx. No user-visible
   staleness results (the anchors must be absent when disabled anyway), and it
   matches base behaviour: the card is rendered once at whatif.html:117 and is
   never OOB-swapped, so the drop/rise inputs themselves also only appear
   after a page reload when the enable checkbox is toggled. Pre-existing
   pattern, not introduced by GV4.
2. Label near-collision with GV2's line (GV2 is foreign, under rework): on a
   30-year plan the card shows "Today: cut ... $839,506.17" while the GV2
   summary shows "... today: $839,796.98" — two different figures, ~$291
   apart, both labelled "today" on the same page. Legitimate per the spec
   (year-0 check vs last-year check deflated), but a reader may read them as
   the same quantity. Worth a wording decision at run level.
3. `gofmt -l .` is dirty for 25 files on base 5fae968 itself under go1.26.6
   (identical list before and after GV4). Pre-existing; `make check` does not
   run gofmt, so it stays green.
